<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_FoundryTowerScatter.xml            UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F4
  ============================================================================
  forge_kit_spec.md F4 "Placement": "reuse the miasma kit's
  RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces with a Forge def-list entry (INVENTED: 0-2 tower
  entrances per Volcano/LavaField-zone map, 0-1 on Pyroclastic skirts)."

  Biome gate — RUT_TheForge only, NOT the three donor defNames the spec
  names (Volcano/LavaField/AB_PyroclasticConflagration). This item's own
  F2/F5/F6 build pass already found, and this pass rechecked directly
  against RUT_TheForge.xml, that BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1 merged all three
  into one owned BiomeDef — the donor defNames back no BiomeDef any map in
  this campaign can actually generate with, so gating on them would be
  gating on dead references, not "using the real biome defNames" the task
  asked for. RUT_TheForge IS the real, live biome defName.

  Count collapse, stated plainly: the spec's own "0-2 Volcano/LavaField vs
  0-1 Pyroclastic" is a split across sub-zones (elevation-based per
  RUT_TheForge.xml's own header: "Volcano median 1,875 m... LavaField median
  2,010 m... Pyroclastic median 1,382 m — all inside this ONE def now"), and
  this def carries no elevation/TileMutatorDef signal to re-derive that
  split from — same situation F5's own edge-band ring already hit and
  collapsed to one uniform biome-wide rate (RUT_ContagionRingScatter.xml's
  own header, read before writing this). This file makes the identical
  collapse, for the identical reason, not a new judgment call: count 2 (the
  higher of the spec's own two figures) is the ceiling for the WHOLE
  biome — GenStep_Scatterer naturally delivers fewer, even zero, on a map
  too small or too crowded to fit that many (its own CalculateFinalCount/
  TryFindScatterCell loop, not a promise). Re-splitting by elevation zone is
  owed to a future pass once a zone signal exists on RUT_TheForge.

  Uses RM_ScattererValidator_Biome (new this pass, src/RimMandrake/
  EnvironmentalHazards/Source/ — see that class's own header) rather than a
  terrain-tag validator (Sump/Contagion's own precedent): RUT_TheForge's own
  terrainsByFertility carries no lava-family terrain of its own (AB_BlackPebbles/
  AB_HardenedGrass only, confirmed reading the raw def this pass) — a
  terrain-based gate would not fire on this biome's own OUTER map at all
  (the melt only exists inside the pocket floor, painted by
  RUT_FoundryFloor_MeltChannels.xml). A direct biome check is therefore the
  correct gate here, not a substitute for one.

  Registered globally onto Base_Player (Patches/
  RUT_FoundryTowerScatter_Register.xml) — safe everywhere per the
  validator's own biome check, same "global registration, self-gating
  GenStepDef" pattern this mod's own RM_GenStep_GradientAxis precedent
  already documents.

  terrainAffordanceNeeded Heavy on the entrance ThingDef itself
  (RUT_FoundryTowerEntrance.xml) is mirrored here via
  ScattererValidator_Buildable's own affordance field, same pairing the
  LanternDeeps mineshaft scatterer (RUT_LanternDeepMineshaft_Scatter.xml)
  already establishes for the identical Heavy-affordance MapPortal shape.

  minSpacing 60 — mirrors the LanternDeeps mineshaft scatterer's own value
  for the same "large, singular set-piece, never clustered" posture; RUT_
  TheForge is a small biome (44 tiles, one compact massif per that def's own
  header), so towers should read as rare landmarks, not a field of them.

  order 322 — one past the LanternDeeps mineshaft scatterer's own 321
  (Patches/RUT_LanternDeepMineshaft_MapGenPatch.xml), same family of
  "portal entrance scatterers" registered on Base_Player, kept adjacent
  rather than picked arbitrarily.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_FoundryTowerScatter</defName>
    <order>322</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces">
      <count>2</count>
      <spotMustBeStandable>true</spotMustBeStandable>
      <minSpacing>60</minSpacing>
      <minEdgeDistPct>0.06</minEdgeDistPct>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
      <validators>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_ScattererValidator_Biome">
          <allowedBiomes>
            <li>RUT_TheForge</li>
          </allowedBiomes>
        </li>
        <li Class="Verse.ScattererValidator_Buildable">
          <affordance>Heavy</affordance>
        </li>
        <li Class="Verse.ScattererValidator_NoNonNaturalEdifices" />
      </validators>
      <elements>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker">
          <markerDef>RUT_FoundryTowerEntrance</markerDef>
        </li>
      </elements>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
